---
const lenses = [
  ['Design', 'copy that needs another pass'],
  ['Product', 'onboarding friction'],
  ['Support', 'tickets that should not exist'],
  ['Engineering', 'edge cases'],
  ['Customer Success', 'repeated explanation'],
  ['Leadership', 'activation, conversion, or data-quality risk'],
];
---

<section id="recognition">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Recognition</div>
    <h2>Your team may already be naming the symptom wrong.</h2>
    <div class="team-lens-grid">
      {lenses.map(([team, symptom]) => (
        <div class="friction-card team-lens-card">
          <strong>{team}</strong>
          <span>{symptom}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="section-copy">
      They may all be paying for the same failure from different budgets: the product asks the user to
      continue before the next move has been made legible.
    </p>
    <div class="method-note">That is where the review begins.</div>
  </div>
</section>
